  "review": {
    "review": "The planner stopped with the hero alive at full health. A mandatory golden key became publicly revealed on a shocking trap at decision 967 (log line 2841). Walking onto it was correctly excluded, but the priority pickup controller had no electrical-clearance action, while mandatory loot suppressed ordinary preparation. Later potion preparation produced invisibility, not the hypothesized levitation. Decisions 1112–1115 recovered the stashed potions; decision 1116 explicitly diagnosed the remaining trapped key before planner exhaustion (lines 3298–3300). The candidate adds a narrowly guarded remote container throw for mandatory loot on revealed shocking plates, accounting for connected-water conduction, and preserves observed-disarm recovery and pickup verification. A public-evidence fixture fails on the original selector and passes on the candidate. The full suite passes 2030 tests with four skipped. This establishes action selection and safety exclusions, not successful key collection or subsequent survival.",
    "learnings": "A required key can need a separate trap-clearance prerequisite. Distinguish an observed safe remote trigger from permission to enter the resulting electricity, and require fresh disarm, effect-expiry and pickup evidence."
